            ("p", "Workplace cameras are normal. Workplace cameras that classify people are a different conversation, and it should happen before the pilot, not after a rumour. Zimbabwe's Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07] (2021) applies to personal data processed by cameras, including images. Expect to need a lawful basis, a defined purpose, minimum necessary collection, a retention limit, and appropriate security."),
            ("p", "Our default design for this kind of system is deliberately conservative: no facial recognition, no identification of individuals, no audio, alerts aggregated by zone and shift rather than attached to a person's name, and raw video not stored at all where inference happens at the edge. Signage at entrances, a written notice to workers and their representatives, and a named contact for questions. This is not legal advice - take local counsel on your obligations - but it is the difference between a deployment that lasts and one that gets switched off."),
            ("h1", "Timeline and budget shape"),
