            ("p", "Fill level is a boundary between liquid and gas. Backlighting turns that boundary into a high-contrast line: light passes through the liquid and the headspace differently, and a camera looking into a diffused panel sees the fill line as a dark or bright edge depending on the product. Front lighting mostly shows you the label and the reflection of the ceiling."),
            ("p", "The best geometry is a camera square to the container, with the container filling 60 to 80 per cent of the frame height, and a diffused backlight panel immediately behind it. A 12 to 25 mm lens on a modern sensor is usually enough. The camera and the light must be rigid relative to the conveyor; a bracket that moves by a millimetre changes the measurement."),
