            ("p", "Roll back first and investigate second when the harm is ongoing, the cause is unclear, and the rollback is cheap. Investigate first only when the rollback itself creates a larger risk - for example, disabling a safety alerting system. Write the decision and the reason in the timeline, even when it turns out to be wrong."),
